{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially","id":1280166,"title":"Scion Mythos officially","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-11T13:15:24-08:00","id":1280166,"title":"Scion Mythos officially","content":"On <a href=\"https://onyxpathcast.podbean.com/e/episode-34-liveish-from-midwinter/\" target=\"_blank\">Mid-Winter Pathcast</a>, it was announced that Onyx Path will create <b>Scion: Masks of Mythos</b> book - Cthulhu Mythos setting for the The World of Scion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-23-2019, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T13:18:50-08:00","id":1280167,"title":"","content":"Welll, that brings me back. Wish I could be part of that, not gonna lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T13:33:38-08:00","id":1280172,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I wonder if they\u2019ll be treated like a playable Pantheon, or just as Titan/Primordial threats the mythic pantheons try to hold the world of humanity up against. Because it\u2019s not like most of them care enough about humanity to play the role of divine patron to a Scion.k","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T13:59:12-08:00","id":1280174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280172#post1280172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... I wonder if they\u2019ll be treated like a playable Pantheon, or just as Titan/Primordial threats the mythic pantheons try to hold the world of humanity up against. Because it\u2019s not like most of them care enough about humanity to play the role of divine patron to a Scion.k</div> </div> </div> </div>Presented as a pantheon, with Scions of their own, per the podcast. How they'll interact with the others is yet to be seen.<br /> <br /> It'll be for a modern-day setting. They'll be working with Chris Spivey, who did <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/218062/Harlem-Unbound\" target=\"_blank\">Harlem Unbound</a>, and the book'll be engaging with the racism of the Mythos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T14:35:56-08:00","id":1280180,"title":"","content":"They were described as a pantheon gone bad (or starting bad, as the case may be)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/453-megazarak","name":"MegaZarak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T16:03:14-08:00","id":1280198,"title":"","content":"A Cthulhu Mythos book announced this early into 2e is a deeply confusing thing to me. Also kind of... weird. I'm trying to stay optimistic, but it's an unexpected and somewhat disappointing pitch, despite the pop culture appeal. I added more extensive thoughts in the blog comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T16:51:35-08:00","id":1280205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280198#post1280198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Cthulhu Mythos book announced this early into 2e is a deeply confusing thing to me. Also kind of... weird. I'm trying to stay optimistic, but it's an unexpected and somewhat disappointing pitch, despite the pop culture appeal. I added more extensive thoughts in the blog comments.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume how early it is is the point - they want to show a range of what Scion can be while the core World setting is also preceding (different people at the helms mean one doesn\u2019t slow down the other).<br /> <br /> That said, the whole thing that Scion is mechanically built around is emulating epic hero myths - and that\u2019s not what Lovecraft narratives are. <br /> <br /> To say nothing of why beings that fundamentally don\u2019t care about humanity at all (save Nyarlathahotep) would empower Scions and involve themselves in the conflicts of humanity\u2019s gods... unless the gods of humanity are Derleth\u2019s Elder Gods who stand against the Outer Gods and Great Old Ones, but of course those were always contrary to Lovecraft\u2019s own themes of a uncaring mad universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-11-2019, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T17:20:28-08:00","id":1280211,"title":"","content":"About the only way I can really see this working is to flip the bird to Lovecraft himself and go all in on Ruthanna Emrys' take on the mythos, with the Deep Ones and similar Mythos beings as persecuted minorities due to both racial and religious prejudice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12492-unseenlibrarian","user":"unseenlibrarian","date":". 01-11-2019, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12492-unseenlibrarian","name":"unseenlibrarian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T20:29:18-08:00","id":1280244,"title":"","content":"I have spoken on this at length why this is distressing in the Discord, and all I will repeat here is I am intensely worried as this goes against what Neall has promised us Scion 2e would be about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T21:40:57-08:00","id":1280255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280205#post1280205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume how early it is is the point - they want to show a range of what Scion can be while the core World setting is also preceding (different people at the helms mean one doesn\u2019t slow down the other).<br /> <br /> That said, the whole thing that Scion is mechanically built around is emulating epic hero myths - and that\u2019s not what Lovecraft narratives are.<br /> <br /> To say nothing of why beings that fundamentally don\u2019t care about humanity at all (save Nyarlathahotep) would empower Scions and involve themselves in the conflicts of humanity\u2019s gods... unless the gods of humanity are Derleth\u2019s Elder Gods who stand against the Outer Gods and Great Old Ones, but of course those were always contrary to Lovecraft\u2019s own themes of a uncaring mad universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>See that last part is what gets me. The uncaring nature and existential threat posed by the Great Old Ones just screams Titan to me, and the source material makes it clear that being related to them makes one kind of monstrous ...<br /> <br /> Didn't Neall mention something about Titan Callings and Knacks with deformities?<br /> <br /> This might be a a Titan book! With playable Titanspawn/Titanborn!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T21:48:09-08:00","id":1280257,"title":"","content":"This is a bad idea, and a dumb one.The Cthulhu Mythos doesn't really fit into what Scion's doing in any way, shape, or form. Maybe as a group of THINGS that some of the other Pantheons look at and go &quot;Titans... I think?&quot;<br /> <br /> Like, even with the stuff Lovecraft wrote, a big part of it was that the Elder Gods he wrote about were largely indifferent to humanity. Part of the thing in Scion is that Gods are, in some way, tied to humanity. They use them to help define themselves.<br /> <br /> The Elder Gods of the Cthulhu Mythos <i>don't</i> care. They're not even antagonistic. They barely notice us. It doesn't quite GEL with how Gods work in Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T22:10:06-08:00","id":1280263,"title":"","content":"Cthulhu mythos don't belong in the scion universe, they're not myth, they're flat fiction invented in the 20th century. Narratively speaking, the inherent assumptions of Lovecraft's setting just flat don't work in Scion as there are tons of similarly cosmic creatures around that people quite easily wrap their heads around. I mean why would Cthulhu, who is essentially an alien high priest, drive you to insanity and yet you are able to comprehend the idea of Inari just fine? Lots of the gods and pantheons are infinitely more layered and counter-intuitive to perceived reality than any of Lovecraft's stuff. For another matter, the mechanics of storypath just flat do not support the cosmic horror aspect of Lovecraft's mythos. Characters are far too competent and powerful and are often as eldritch as any Lovecraftian entity.<br /> <br /> A cthulhu book of creatures from various pantheons that may have inspired Lovecraft's writings, maybe, but as a full pantheon it seems offensive to the real world cultures included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T04:42:29-08:00","id":1280294,"title":"","content":"I was enthused when I heard this on the podcast. I'm interested to see their take on it. Some people here are forgetting that there's an Atlantean (sp) pantheon. Those gods are no more or less fictional than the Cthulhu mythos. I believe Eddy said in the podcast that they wanted to explore a &quot;bad pantheon&quot; without using a real world religion and drawing controversy for doing it.<br /> <br /> As for why it's been announced so early, I think it's because these books take so long to come out that by the time we get it it won't be early anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":1277,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","user":"karpomatic","date":". 01-12-2019, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T05:35:13-08:00","id":1280303,"title":"","content":"I don't know, people. I know far too much about Lovecraft themes and I can see where the doubts comes from, but I'm confident that if the developers decided to announce this book they have something solid and different to build it upon. Something that goes further than picking up Cthulhu and dropping it screaming from the sky into the Scion setting.<br /> <br /> I think there's a passage we can't possibly know about right now that will make things interesting and not too heretical at the very least.<br /> <br /> Also, and here I'll be brief because I'd write for hours if I don't, not all works featuring the Mythos have to play the Cosmic Horror aspect absolutely straight to have a reason to be. It's been 100 years. Lovecraft's dead, he was ok with people having fun with his works even when alive and, I'm saying this as someone that owes <i>a lot</i> to him, he can also go fuck himself for several good reasons. I regularly visit his tomb, bring flowers and pay homage to it, but the author is dead.<br /> <br /> That stuff has become part of the popular culture enough to allow different takes. We can have Ligotti, Laird Barron and Junji Ito just as we can have Ruthanna Emrys, Jordan Peele, Matt Ruff and Edgar Cantero (Stephen King just watches from the side, doing his thing). True Detective, IT, Hellboy and Bloodborne are all good for different reasons and with different styles.<br /> <br /> Scion has all the tools it needs to make something decent with the Mythos, though I admit I have no idea how the final result will look.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents about it, but I think the writers can do it and make a good work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-12-2019, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T05:59:07-08:00","id":1280308,"title":"","content":"The announcement of this book is equal parts distressing and baffling to me. I was hoping with the write up of the Atlanteans would have been the end of the fictional Pantheons, but this just went form bad to so so much worse. There are so many Pantheons out there that deserve a write up, so many cool Gods and Myths and People that would love to share them, so many nooks and crannies of the world yet to be explored... and we get this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T10:08:01-08:00","id":1280339,"title":"","content":"As someone who likes to game, i'm excited for this. I have tried everything to get my group to look into and/or play CoCthulu without success. They don't want to learn another(especially an older) system. We have ChoD, WoD, D&amp;D 3.5/Pathfinder, Cin. Unisystem, and now Storypath. What I don't understand is why there is so much negativity and &quot;wrong game think&quot;. There are multiple books already being written, and most if not all are gonna have &quot;Your pantheon which is totez best&quot; and they will attempt to treat them with as much respect as the others. But like Karpomatic said repeating or paraphrasing Eddy &quot;We want to do a bad pantheon without attacking anyone's actual religion or history&quot;. Save the hate bashing for after you have more than a one sentence idea to run off of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T10:22:34-08:00","id":1280346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280339#post1280339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who likes to game, i'm excited for this. I have tried everything to get my group to look into and/or play CoCthulu without success. They don't want to learn another(especially an older) system. We have ChoD, WoD, D&amp;D 3.5/Pathfinder, Cin. Unisystem, and now Storypath. What I don't understand is why there is so much negativity and &amp;quot;wrong game think&amp;quot;. There are multiple books already being written, and most if not all are gonna have &amp;quot;Your pantheon which is totez best&amp;quot; and they will attempt to treat them with as much respect as the others. But like Karpomatic said repeating or paraphrasing Eddy &amp;quot;We want to do a bad pantheon without attacking anyone's actual religion or history&amp;quot;. Save the hate bashing for after you have more than a one sentence idea to run off of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally i\u2019m fine with it as long as it\u2019s isolated to this sourcebook, because I trust the people who they\u2019ve mentioned working on it or having some degree of consulting role. But I also get why other people would have a viscserally negative \u201cyou can\u2019t work your ass off to afford real religions\u2019 gods respect in a game\u2019s framework and then turn around and apply that same framework to the make-believe of a virulent racist he created specifically to embody many of his paranoias about the very believers those real religions\u2019 gods are sacred to! That completely devalues said framework as respectful\u201d reaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T10:41:48-08:00","id":1280353,"title":"","content":"I wasn't introduced to Lovecraft until I started gaming in the 8th grade, so this racism bit is lost on me. I really only know about his stuff via the games, and like I said, my group has never entertained learning a system that has mythos stuff, so if it's detailed in the game books, i've missed that part too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T10:53:24-08:00","id":1280355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManBearPig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280353#post1280353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't introduced to Lovecraft until I started gaming in the 8th grade, so this racism bit is lost on me. I really only know about his stuff via the games, and like I said, my group has never entertained learning a system that has mythos stuff, so if it's detailed in the game books, i've missed that part too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to get into the details, but Lovecraft was so racist that he was considered the lunatic racist in a time period where being racist was very normal. He was so racist that other racists in his own era thought he was way too racist. You can notice it in how a lot of the fears expressed in his works are about 'interbreeding' between different 'species' and so on and so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T11:02:01-08:00","id":1280358,"title":"","content":"I'm firmly in the disappointed category. Mythos stuff is so over-done these days that this amounts to a pantheon supplement about memes. There are dozens of real-world pantheons and hundreds (thousands) of deities that could be detailed, so why go for a completely fictional group of beings that care nothing for humanity at all? It's been done to death in RPGs already (Call of Cthulhu, Cthulhutech, GURPS Cthulhupunk, Delta Green, and more) so why bother going there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T11:05:05-08:00","id":1280360,"title":"","content":"There's an opportunity in that. The most beautiful Lovecraft-inspired things of the last decade pretty much all come from authors that turned subverted, burned down and scattered to the winds that kind of racist garbage that tainted the mind of the man. All stuff that reclaims what's good about the Mythos and discards the rest, often while giving it a middle finger before doing so. It's both right and poetically appropriate. Scion can do that too.<br /> <br /> Cosmic Horror does not need to reflect Lovecraft's racism in the slightest. That's not what gives it strength, otherwise we would not be here talking about it. The duty for all those that tackle with it is to recognize why people like Lovecraft, why people hate it (rightfully so, mind you) and then move forward and improve.<br /> <br /> The genre is not Lovecraft. He may have created it, but he has no rights over it.<br /> <br /> Ride Cthulhu into the future and have it devour those who are in the room for the racist propaganda instead than the eldritch wonder.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T11:07:57-08:00","id":1280361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280355#post1280355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to get into the details, but Lovecraft was so racist that he was considered the lunatic racist in a time period where being racist was very normal. He was so racist that other racists in his own era thought he was way too racist. You can notice it in how a lot of the fears expressed in his works are about 'interbreeding' between different 'species' and so on and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah<br /> <br /> - Shadow Over Innsmouth is entirely about Lovecraft\u2019s fear of \u201crace mixing\u201d<br /> <br /> - The primary active threat in Call of Cthulhu is the savage debauched cult of black and native peoples<br /> <br /> - Mountain of Madness is about how an oppressed class gaining social equality led to the decline and obliteration of a once mighty and proud civilization<br /> <br /> and so on.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying \u201cand therefor people can\u2019t like Lovecraf\u2019s work!\u201d You can enjoy CS Lewis without being Christian. You can enjoy Rudyard Kipling without being an Imperialist. But as with their philsophical identities, Lovecraft\u2019s racism is in the dna of his work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-12-2019, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T11:09:18-08:00","id":1280362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280358#post1280358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm firmly in the disappointed category. Mythos stuff is so over-done these days that this amounts to a pantheon supplement about memes. There are dozens of real-world pantheons and hundreds (thousands) of deities that could be detailed, so why go for a completely fictional group of beings that care nothing for humanity at all? It's been done to death in RPGs already (Call of Cthulhu, Cthulhutech, GURPS Cthulhupunk, Delta Green, and more) so why bother going there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason there\u2019s so many: it sells and it\u2019s public domain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T11:11:19-08:00","id":1280363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280360#post1280360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an opportunity in that. The most beautiful Lovecraft-inspired things of the last decade pretty much all come from authors that turned subverted, burned down and scattered to the winds that kind of racist garbage that tainted the mind of the man. All stuff that reclaims what's good about the Mythos and discards the rest, often while giving it a middle finger before doing so. It's both right and poetically appropriate. Scion can do that too.<br /> <br /> Cosmic Horror does not need to reflect Lovecraft's racism in the slightest. That's not what gives it strength, otherwise we would not be here talking about it. The duty for all those that tackle with it is to recognize why people like Lovecraft, why people hate it (rightfully so, mind you) and then move forward and improve.<br /> <br /> The genre is not Lovecraft. He may have created it, but he has no rights over it.<br /> <br /> Ride Cthulhu into the future and have it devour those who are in the room for the racist propaganda instead than the eldritch wonder.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why i\u2019d rather an original Cosmic Horror fictional pantheon, influenced by Lovecraft the way the Atlanteans are going to be Jack Kirby influenced, but not using Lovecraft\u2019s own creations.<br /> <br /> But I realize that won\u2019t sell as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T11:31:17-08:00","id":1280366,"title":"","content":"Also, there is the whole problem of false equivalencies. Firstly, the &quot;gods&quot; of the Lovecraftian cosmos do not scale with the gods of world mythology. Whereas myths are always about humanity and what it can and cannot achieve in some way, Lovecraft's beings are intented to be creatures of pure science, even the science mysterious to and beyond humanity; they do not care and there is no magic to them, they are the stuff the universe, the tangible, scientific universe is made of. Depending on how you read them, they are either infinitely beyond the gods of mythology, being present in multiple dimensions and on far off planets whereas the gods of real-world mythology are confined to earth and its closest neighbours, or infinetely below them, seeing as both Elder Things and boats were able to throw down with Cthulhu whereas Vishnu or Olodumare would be literally omnipotent, omnipresent, and omniscient. And that's not even getting into how they fit into categories like God, Titan, and Primordial (spoiler alert: They don't.)<br /> <br /> Secondly, there is the ethical issue. Scion, especially in its vastly improved 2e incarnation, is a game that is about honouring the beings of world religions and world mythologies, even though it may be in an unconventional way. With the way particularly the Deva, Manitou, and Orisha were written, there is a flavour of decolonisation, of amending what has been done wrong in the past to it all. The mere inclusion of the Lovecraftian &quot;deities&quot; <i>no matter how it is done</i> spits in the face of that for the very simple fact that it creates an equivalency between the beings sacred to millions of people and the consciously fantastical creations of a single person, creations meant to inspire horror, not devotion, and to express his personal ideologies, not the shared values of grand cultures. And that is doubly horrifying because it creates an equivalency between the most sacred things of denigrated peoples of colour and the pet OCs of a man who was very much disgusted by these &quot;inferior races&quot;, who wrote his stories with the express intention of warning about and exploiting for tantalising entertainment the perceived &quot;degeneracy&quot; of these peoples.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I love the Lovecraft Mythos, and I love the things that can be done with it. But here it does not belong. Here, it can only do harm. And whoever has conceived of this should know that not only will I never put money into a supplement like this, it makes me question putting money into the Scion line as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T11:56:55-08:00","id":1280371,"title":"","content":"I'm slightly optimistic if all Cthulhu Mythos Great Old Ones are Titans, or even Primordials. They are so removed from humanity, they <b>should not</b> be Gods, in Scion sense. ( As Lovecraftian horror fan, I'm interested to see what comes from this supplement. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T11:59:03-08:00","id":1280372,"title":"","content":"I won't argue about the inclusion of a Mythos Pantheon and how it has <i>very nasty</i> implications about things, about how it puts legitimate deities of real world religions up against a collection of fictional figures many of whom are based off these real figures (Nodens, Dagon, etc) and were popularized by a man who thought that the people who worshiped these real deities were backwards, horrible, and 'savage.' There is no argument there, it's plain as day why that is just very.... much an issue. Maybe they could resolve it, but what I would instead like to focus on is the themes of the two genres involved.<br /> <br /> Scion is a game based on Heroic Sagas and similar texts, and its themes directly clash against those of the Mythos. Hopelessness, the inevitability of loss, the fundamental inevitability of failure, those are not the themes of Scion. Scion is a game not about 'Will You Succeed?' but a game about 'How Will You Succeed?' There is a fundamental thematic clash here, not even in the sense of 'these two Pantheons have a different thematic focus' but in a 'These are directly opposites' notion. <br /> <br /> The horror of the Mythos, the realization that you are but gnats in the face of uncaring beings of unimaginable power... well that's cut short by the other Pantheons. Nyame is here, and he is Omnipotent, and a very nice friendly person who wants to see you succeed. YHWH is around and while He has some days of being a bit eldritch, He tends to care either that you're being good or being bad. There is borderline a limitless continuation of this list, of beings that exist in Scion that just cut the legs out from the horror that the Mythos expresses. Sure, there's <i>one</i> Pantheon that is all about the hopelessness of humanity, but then you're a M\u00edlisian and you can can kill Gods really easily so that.... hard to not have hope when you have Deicide in your blood.<br /> <br /> Sure, Azathoth is huge and colossal and when he wakes reality will end, but... that's like Tuesday for the Pantheons. If Atum-Re blinks reality ends, it's really not an uncommon theme, and honestly, you should be way more worried about Atum-Re blinking since Apep is actively trying to eat him every night than the possibility that Azathoth might wake up one day. And, because the Scion system is based on the three 'tiers' of Divinity, Gods, Titans, and Primordials, this means that Azathoth is equal to other Primordials. So throw M\u00edl Esp\u00e1ine at anything from the Mythos, and he could cut them down like chaff, and he's literally a random human who brought on a deicide, the ancestor of humanity equal to Danu for the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 Danann. Hard to not have hope. Especially when this is a 'One Pantheon v. Literally Every Pantheon Humanity Has Ever Worshiped' situation.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, if these Mythos Figures are intended to be an antagonistic Pantheon... why didn't they get their shit stomped? Because, as I have spoken about at length before, actual like reality-ending threats are not something any Pantheon wants. It's not something the vast majority of Titans want, or Primordials. So, if this one Pantheon is being actively malignant and opposed to everyone else... I mean, sure they're strong like any Pantheon is, but they're contesting against every Titan, Primordial, and God from every Pantheon ever. Countless numbers of omipotent beings would just turn on them.<br /> <br /> The idea of including the Mythos is an act of respect to not turn a real Pantheon into an 'evil Pantheon' is also totally missing the forest for the trees. You are legitimizing this 'Pantheon' as much as the Hindu Gods, you are making them equally true, and... like, if this is coming from a place of respect, that feels fundamentally misguided and very badly thought out.<br /> <br /> Now, there is a place for Cosmic Horror in Scion, but not this sort of cosmic horror. Apotheosis is a horror story for most Pantheons. If you are a Theoi Scion, you are no longer a 'person,' you are an abstract concept that most of the time wears a people suit. If you are a Netjer or Deva Scion, congratulations, you have lost your individuality. You are no longer a 'person.' A Netjer Scion will find their 'self' broken into shards and find that they never manifest in a 'pure' form, but always find themselves as an being comprised of at least one other 'person.' You are no longer Tim, you are Tim-Seth-Ra, but you are also Seth-Tim-Bes, and you are Kephri-Tim-Atum and you all exist at the same time and are having a conversation where you all visceral disagree with each other. For the Deva you are a shard of the infinite, and... you just aren't an individual any more.<br /> <br /> There is place for true cosmic horror in Scion, but it's not this without <i>heavily</i> compromising either the themes of Scion, or the themes of the Mythos. Lovecraftan material is cool, but this feels like literally the diametrically opposite place that it belongs. I hope this turns out to be some sort of internal miscommunication, as it goes against everything that 2e has done to be respectful and well researched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T12:17:35-08:00","id":1280381,"title":"","content":"I mean... there should be room to use Scion to do Shards with fictional gods - fictional author-invented mythologies, religions, and deities are a fantasy staple that Scion is absolutely suited to playing with such epics as well as its real mythologies. But I would keep those to their own Shards.<br /> <br /> It would work better if the Mythos book wasn\u2019t \u201coptionally part of the World\u201d, but rather presented a full on separate Shard where Cthulhu isn\u2019t hanging out with actual sacred deities.<br /> <br /> Besides devaluing the gods of the World - co-existing with the Gods also make Lovecraftian horror hooks completely unachievable. The existence of the afterlives of Legend completely defeat the finite materialism of human existence that Lovecraft was playing off of. Fate means life isn\u2019t just random happenstance. Etc etc.<br /> <br /> That said, as long as it remains bound in its single source book and stays out of other products (especially Demigod and God) I don\u2019t have a big problem with its existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T12:30:30-08:00","id":1280383,"title":"","content":"Also, this may not be a universal opinion, but the Lovecraft Elder Gods are <b><i>BORING</i></b> if you put them in any context other than as clumsy metaphors for man's ambiguous existential dread.<br /> <br /> Like, maybe a Storypath Hack for Cthulhu might work. I have no interest in it but sure, that's fine.<br /> <br /> <b>Keep it out of my Scion</b>, for fuck's sake. If you MUST make a Scion Cthulhu Writeup, then I insist that the first chapter be a breakdown of how much of a racist fuck Lovecraft was, and a breakdown of how his bundle of neuroses informed literally all his work, and then fill an entire page with &quot;THIS IS NOT CANON WITH MAINLINE SCION&quot; stamps.<br /> <br /> In fact if I can just <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5\" data-vbnamecard=\"5\">RichT</a> here... Rich, I think that Scion: Mythos is a mistake, and a gross misuse of the line's resources. I would, as a buyer and a guy who backed the Origin and Hero books, suggest you <i>rethink this</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T18:39:36-08:00","id":1280426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280294#post1280294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was enthused when I heard this on the podcast. I'm interested to see their take on it. Some people here are forgetting that there's an Atlantean (sp) pantheon. </div> </div> </div> </div>The differences are:<br /> <br /> 1. The Atlantean Pantheon is going to be non-canon, included in the Companion as a very much admitted up front fictional Pantheon that is very much optional.<br /> <br /> 2. The Atlantean Pantheon is going to be designed as Y'know actual gods. With character, worship traditions, and the semblance of a culture associated with them.<br /> <br /> The crew are going to make an effort to have the Atlantean Gods fit into the tone that Scion has: That of modern myth and heroics, by way of crystal magical nanotech.<br /> <br /> The Elder Gods and Great Old Ones exist as a metaphor for how uncaring the universe is, and how ultimately humans are utterly insignificant. That is what makes them scary to many people: Because they remind humans of how small we are.<br /> <br /> <i>This tone is completely at odds with what Scion does</i>.<br /> <br /> And even if you do put in an Evil/Uncaring Pantheon (why would they make Scions?) you have the other problem that Cthulhu and co make for very poor additions to a Scion game. Cthulhu has no real powers beyond &quot;big&quot; and &quot;tough to kill... For a lowly human&quot;. Cthulhu doesn't demonstrate any kind of mythic ability. It's not a god, it's a giant squid thing. Correct me if I'm wrong, but I don't believe that the whole &quot;to look upon Cthulhu is to be driven mad&quot; is meant to be some kind of indication of a special power and more that humans can't comprehend the creature we're looking upon.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why Call of Cthulhu's character types are priests, scientists, historians, and gruff salty fishermen. These are ordinary people, people poking at things their delicate minds can't comprehend. If they poke too deeply or learn too much, they're doomed. A shoggoth could take them out.<br /> <br /> Sic a shoggoth on a Hero with the Warrior Calling and they'll tear it apart. In the context of comparing Cthulhu to Zeus, Law and Order and Lightning wearing a person suit, or Shiva with the third eye whose gaze can vaporize the world (but won't because Sarasvati took the world-ending flames and ate them), or even Ogma telling this squid thing to get off his lawn... Yeah, in mythic terms Cthulhu's a chump.<br /> <br /> So yeah, like I said. Cthulhu? A puss-poor fit for a game like Scion, and offering little Call of Cthulhu fans will enjoy. Like part of the reason you play Call of Cthulhu is for the horror angle.<br /> <br /> Scion would not work well for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T18:57:18-08:00","id":1280430,"title":"","content":"Cthulhu is small potatoes within the context of Lovecraft mythos. The most powerful entity in Lovecraft, Azathoth, is still not really much compared to the bizarre natures of many of the entities in the pantheons already included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T05:10:24-08:00","id":1280461,"title":"","content":"If I may put my two cents on this whole point:<br /> <br /> I think, as it was announced, that was a poor choice. I am all up to create a pantheon for Cthulhu, but after all books are released and they go on and say: &quot;Okay, we are making a brief pause of deeply researched and historically sensitive pantheons to make something fun and easier.&quot; and make an extra book, absolute off canon, with a few fictional pantheons, like publish the Mythos with the Tolkien Pantheon, Basic D&amp;D Pantheon (Pelor and so forth) and Disney Pantheon. They might even make like a public vote to see which pantheons they will choose.<br /> <br /> Create those pantheons, but make they separated form regular world. Like a fun, uncomplicated way to play Scion in different Tones: wanna play it darker and hopeless, go for Cthulhu. Wanna play it more fantasy like, go for D&amp;D pantheon. Wanna play it all fairy tale, go for Disney. I have no idea of how they would rebuild those concepts to fit in a working world, but I have all faith they could do it, and would make less people pissed off because those would be separated, self-sufficient worlds. And we would not need to compare the validity of the Mythos with the Greek Gods, for example, because it would be published very obviously as non canon, together with the Great Goddess Ariel, ruler of the Sea and Mistress of all that Sings.<br /> <br /> But right now, saying they want to do the Mythos, while fans are making their own pantheons books because they really wanna those pantheons but they are not famous enough to be on the top of the priority list (By the way, thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13670-svarogg\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13670_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13670\" data-vbnamecard=\"13670\">Svarogg</a> and all of you guys), specially considering the whole implications of comparing real-life and fictional pantheons, sounds like a bad idea. Plus, if they make it before Demigod and God gone out, they will need to finish it in other supplement.<br /> <br /> About the racism, they can sanitized it, like every other media. The racism is present, but if you change a few things, mostly minor, the racism is just metaphorical enough to not be too noticeable. Most people who did not study about Lovecraft will not notice, and people who did will never be able to forget anyway. Specially because the Older Gods are everything but racist, as they do not care about humans, no matter where is your ancestry from. Which by itself creates a problem for why would they create Scions, but that is another topic.<br /> <br /> Im not commenting on what was said, as I have not heard the podcast, just the idea to start working on a Mythos book right now. I also will not comment the &quot;a pantheon gone bad&quot;, because I would argue that no pantheon has gone &quot;right&quot;, in the sense that they are not all good people. If they mean bad as in, &quot;Evil, wants to destroy the world&quot;, which is an interesting concept, just fake a pantheon. Say that an Ancient population had those gods, the population was extinct and just the Gods remained, and now they want to destroy the world because of it. Hell, just create a variation of the Atlantean Pantheon, say that that the Atlanteans all died for whatever reason (war, earthquake due to Poseidon, Hubris or whatever) and now the Atlanteans Gods are all evil.<br /> <br /> --No one will be comparing fictional to real mythology, as the Atlanteans are already a fictional not-really-canon Gods that everybody is okay with,<br /> <br /> --No racism to sanitized,<br /> <br /> --Still fits the previously created cosmology and tone in a way that is easy to insert/remove then,<br /> <br /> --Has precedents, as the Nementedevos is also a Pantheon which population has mostly disappeared,<br /> <br /> --And, at least in my view, is actually more interesting than the regular Atlanteans. I never cared about the Atlanteans before, but if they were an evil Pantheon lurking around to recreate evil cults and trying to destroy all Pantheons, I would be far more interested.<br /> <br /> And before anybody says that some people still wants their Atlantean Pantheon, I say: just create a variation. Then we have good Atlanteans for those who want, bad Atlanteans for those who want, they can try the &quot;Pantheon gone bad&quot; concept without pissing anybody off, and everybody is happy. Then make the Mythos later, as a fun &quot;not-canon&quot; supplement, so they can also have the appeal of putting the Mythos into the Scion Series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12934,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","user":"Manbat","date":". 01-13-2019, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T09:22:14-08:00","id":1280494,"title":"","content":"I definitely understand everyone's issues with the idea of this addition, but I have to ask? This is a supplement, right? Seems to me if you don't want the Cthulhu mythos in Scion, simply don't buy the supplement and include it in your games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T12:54:42-08:00","id":1280535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280494#post1280494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely understand everyone's issues with the idea of this addition, but I have to ask? This is a supplement, right? Seems to me if you don't want the Cthulhu mythos in Scion, simply don't buy the supplement and include it in your games?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean yes, but that supplement doesn't come from nowhere. That will cost the writers time, time for research, time for writing, and will cost OPP money to pay those writers for their time and their words.<br /> <br /> Those costs, IMO, could be allocated better, on basically anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T13:16:48-08:00","id":1280538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280535#post1280535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean yes, but that supplement doesn't come from nowhere. That will cost the writers time, time for research, time for writing, and will cost OPP money to pay those writers for their time and their words.<br /> <br /> Those costs, IMO, could be allocated better, on basically anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Yeah, that is something to consider. I mean, we have laundry lists of real Pantheons we want made. That should be a higher priority than bringing another fictional Pantheon in and giving it the full book treatment. The Atlantean Pantheon is okay because it's just being used as an example on how to build a Pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T13:52:37-08:00","id":1280543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280535#post1280535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean yes, but that supplement doesn't come from nowhere. That will cost the writers time, time for research, time for writing, and will cost OPP money to pay those writers for their time and their words.<br /> <br /> Those costs, IMO, could be allocated better, on basically anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019d likely rebut that a likelier strong seller given the track record of Mythos products in the rpg market, will generate more revenue to do more things that you and I want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T14:35:41-08:00","id":1280555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MegaZarak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280180#post1280180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were described as a pantheon gone bad (or starting bad, as the case may be)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What the hell is a &quot;pantheon gone bad?&quot;<br /> <br /> Looking at the track record of these various religions from a modern viewpoint, and the majority of them aren't exactly people who inspire reverence.<br /> <br /> Still, I like the idea of a Lovecraft style pantheon being introduced to the mix, especially since it introduces a more scientific aspect to the creation mythos. Humanity didn't just spring into existence one day, it happened over the course of millions of years, as the gods continued to experiment with biology and seeding new life across the cosmos.<br /> <br /> I'm also curious how they'll be portraying the abject nihilism found in Lovecraft's cosmology. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280308#post1280308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The announcement of this book is equal parts distressing and baffling to me. I was hoping with the write up of the Atlanteans would have been the end of the fictional Pantheons, but this just went form bad to so so much worse. There are so many Pantheons out there that deserve a write up, so many cool Gods and Myths and People that would love to share them, so many nooks and crannies of the world yet to be explored... and we get this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta be careful with deciding what qualifies as a fictional pantheon, since those who aren't exactly religious would easily claim that all religions are the work of fiction. The only thing that separates Lovecraft from Zeus and Odin is that his work originates from a more recent point in our history.<br /> <br /> Heck, the same thing could be said about Mormonism and Scientology, two religions which are less than 400 years old, and yet regarded as legitimate faiths by people throughout the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-13-2019, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T16:04:13-08:00","id":1280566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280555#post1280555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta be careful with deciding what qualifies as a fictional pantheon, since those who aren't exactly religious would easily claim that all religions are the work of fiction. The only thing that separates Lovecraft from Zeus and Odin is that his work originates from a more recent point in our history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are conflating definitions here: it is fictional pantheons in the meaning that those pantheons are tied and have been created in works of fiction, and real pantheons are those tied to real religions that exist/existed in real life. Nobody is saying, at least here, that Zeus exist in real life, but that the belief of Zeus existed in real life.<br /> <br /> Not wanting to get into the clear differences between the creation of a real and a fictional pantheon, it is not about existing, it is about being worshiped, is about people believing on it. No one as a cultural group worshiped the Mythos. I dont think anyone would argue that the Mythos actually exist, or that they form a religion in any reasonable definition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280555#post1280555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, the same thing could be said about Mormonism and Scientology, two religions which are less than 400 years old, and yet regarded as legitimate faiths by people throughout the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not about age, it is about belief, worship, is about dedication, be it sacrifices, time, money and love for years, if not entire lives. Is about shaping lives, communities and minds. Most Ancient religions are, of course, very old, but newer religions are no less &quot;real&quot; to those who believe because they are new, and their sacrifices are no less valuable<br /> <br /> And, as a personal note, even as an atheist non-religious myself, I understand why some people are baffled by this announcement, and why some would even consider disrespect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T17:57:40-08:00","id":1280583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manbat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280566#post1280566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you are conflating definitions here: it is fictional pantheons in the meaning that those pantheons are tied and have been created in works of fiction, and real pantheons are those tied to real religions that exist/existed in real life. Nobody is saying, at least here, that Zeus exist in real life, but that the belief of Zeus existed in real life.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I said, the only thing separating Lovecraft's works from those of the &quot;real&quot; pantheons is the time gap between their creations. In fact, I came across some information years ago talking about how there is a particularly avid group of fans who are trying to make The Force a fully recognized faith. So does that mean that we should include the likes of the Celestials, or Abeloth into Scion, as there are actually people in our world who worship such things?<br /> <br /> From an atheistic stand point, all religions are fictional. They haven't existed since the dawn of time, somebody had to go out of their way to create them from the ground up. A long, long time ago, some people who didn't understand the world came up with whatever excuse they could think of to explain the nature of the universe and preached these ideas to those around them. Eventually, those ideas grew to become the religions they are known for today. All it takes is time, and enough people willing to agree to the idea for a religion to form.<br /> <br /> In fact, one could argue that it's already happening, as more and more people are starting to take inspiration from Lovecraft's mythos over the years, both in mainstream media, as well as the less popularized works.<br /> <br /> <br /> And on that note, I would say the idea of a religion founded on existential dread and nihilism is totally relevant to the world we live in today. Far more relevant, in fact, than praising a shape shifting rapist, just because he killed the embodiment of time and took over his throne. People are smarter in this day and age than they have ever been, and along with that newfound intellect comes a host of knowledge that both inspires and terrifies us.<br /> <br /> Theories like the Big Crunch, and Heat Death warn that the universe is ultimately finite and will eventually come to an end, along with all life within it. While the impossibility of FTL travel means that humanity will most likely never colonize beyond our solar system. Lovecraft had it right on the money, humanity is insignificant. Nothing we do matters, because the universe is more vast than we can possibly fathom, and anything we create will ultimately crumble to dust in time.<br /> <br /> That's the major point about Lovecraft's work that I find so fascinating. Regardless of what his political and cultural views may have been, his philosophy on cosmic horror makes perfect sense to me. And I am very curious to see how White Wolf plans to implement such concepts into Scion going forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T18:10:45-08:00","id":1280585,"title":"","content":"(Sorry for the double post)<br /> <br /> And once again, I'd like to point out more recent and &quot;real&quot; religions like Mormonism.<br /> <br /> According to their faith, Satan is Jesus' brother, and when we all die, we have a chance to become gods of our own planets.<br /> <br /> Now, obviously, this completely contradicts more popular forms of Christianity, but it's still a fully recognized faith that's worshiped by people all over the world. And since the existence of YHVH was stated to be true earlier in this very topic, we have to question which version of the story is canon to Scion. Is Satan Jesus' brother, or is he an angel who fell from grace? Do we join YHVH in Heaven for eternity, or do we become creator deities of our own worlds?<br /> <br /> <br /> And then there's Scientology, which tells that the reason for us being unhappy is because we have tortured alien souls trapped inside us, which were frozen in ice and then dropped into volcanoes by Boeing 747's that flew across the cosmos on orders by the evil tyrant, Xenu!<br /> <br /> You want to try fitting that creation mythos into the Scion universe? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-13-2019, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T18:50:44-08:00","id":1280589,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> - ... Did you seriously just try and compare an actual living religion to Lovecraft's rantings? Did you seriously imply that both are equally fictional?<br /> <br /> Dude I don't practice any religions at all and I just gotta say <b>the actual fuck, dude?</b><br /> <br /> Anyway, if they do do this supplement I prefer that they make it its own separate shard, kept far away from Mainline Scion. The Elder Gods and Great Old Ones do not form thematically and lose basically all their teeth and impact compared to basically all the Pantheons.<br /> <br /> Also, re Mormanism and Scientology. At my table i'd paint the Heavenly Angelic Host as having no comment on the Church of Latter Day Saints.<br /> <br /> And Scientology in Scion is a scam, just as it is in the World. A scam that was made up by a sci fi author who has on record noted that Religion is a perfect scam","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T18:55:44-08:00","id":1280591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280589#post1280589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> - ... Did you seriously just try and compare an actual living religion to Lovecraft's rantings? Did you seriously imply that both are equally fictional?<br /> <br /> Dude I don't practice any religions at all and I just gotta say <b>the actual fuck, dude?</b><br /> <br /> Anyway, if they do do this supplement I prefer that they make it its own separate shard, kept far away from Mainline Scion. The Elder Gods and Great Old Ones do not form thematically and lose basically all their teeth and impact compared to basically all the Pantheons.<br /> <br /> Also, re Mormanism and Scientology. At my table i'd paint the Heavenly Angelic Host as having no comment on the Church of Latter Day Saints.<br /> <br /> And Scientology in Scion is a scam, just as it is in the World. A scam that was made up by a sci fi author who has on record noted that Religion is a perfect scam</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I was trying to point out the fact that people on this thread are calling Lovecraft's writings a &quot;fake&quot; religion, and referencing the fact that not everybody believes in religion. So from their point of view, all religions would be made up, or the work of fantasy. I'm honestly confused as to why people are drawing lines between Lovecraft's work, and the works of these other pantheons, when there are millions of people in the world who honestly don't see any difference between them.<br /> <br /> You say that Scientology is a scam, and yet it seems to meet the qualifications of what was previously stated to be recognized as a religion. In the sense that people actually worship it, and it shapes their ideology and so forth. By calling it a false religion, you are not only contradicting a prior explanation of what a 'real' religion is, but you're also disrespecting the people who believe in it.<br /> <br /> Wasn't trying to be offensive. Just pointing out an important piece of information that I feel like everybody was overlooking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-13-2019, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T19:04:41-08:00","id":1280592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280591#post1280591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, I was trying to point out the fact that people on this thread are calling Lovecraft's writings a &quot;fake&quot; religion, and referencing the fact that not everybody believes in religion. So from their point of view, all religions would be made up, or the work of fantasy. I'm honestly confused as to why people are drawing lines between Lovecraft's work, and the works of these other pantheons, when there are millions of people in the world who honestly don't see any difference between them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because when we talk about &quot;real religion&quot; we aren't making a statement about metaphysical accuracy. We're talking about the sociological reality of a cultural belief system grown over time and actually practiced by people in real life either currently or historically (or historically and then reconstructed). There is no comparison between a sociologically real religion and Lovecraft's fiction. Unknowable metaphysical realities are irrelevant to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T19:15:28-08:00","id":1280593,"title":"","content":"The thing is that we've got things like Hinduism, Shinto, and Buddhism in the game right now. It's one thing to tell those people that their beliefs are being treated with the same respect as the beliefs of other cultures that have been in some way assimilated, it's something completely different to come in and say that it's on the same level as the writings of some misanthropic racist from the 1920s. It doesn't matter if you're trying to be offensive or not, what matters is how you respond when you're called out on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T19:22:32-08:00","id":1280594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280592#post1280592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because when we talk about &quot;real religion&quot; we aren't making a statement about metaphysical accuracy. We're talking about the sociological reality of a cultural belief system grown over time and actually practiced by people in real life either currently or historically (or historically and then reconstructed). There is no comparison between a sociologically real religion and Lovecraft's fiction. Unknowable metaphysical realities are irrelevant to that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And as I said, the only difference between Lovecraft and the other religions is time. The actual bible wasn't written and codified until 30 years after Jesus' death. The idea of cosmic horror and us living in a cold, uncaring universe is becoming increasingly more prevalent over the years. Two of the most popular cartoons in recent history (Rick and Morty, and Bojack Horseman) heavily revolve around these concepts as the focus of their series.<br /> <br /> And I've lost count of how many times I've seen eldritch beings inspired by Lovecraft's works being depicted in other forms of media and entertainment. Almost always being described as deities, or at least something of relatively similar power. Even if they don't outright worship Lovecraft's mythology, the fact remains that they are so popular, that they're beginning to spread everywhere, and with increasing frequency.<br /> <br /> So if you're idea of a religion is something that shapes people's sociological reality and cultural belief, I once again say that it is only a matter of time. Existential nihilism is becoming more and more common, and we have no way of predicting how it will turn out in future. So shooting it down as a fake religion is a little premature from my perspective.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutoDefenestrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280593#post1280593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is that we've got things like Hinduism, Shinto, and Buddhism in the game right now. It's one thing to tell those people that their beliefs are being treated with the same respect as the beliefs of other cultures that have been in some way assimilated, it's something completely different to come in and say that it's on the same level as the writings of some misanthropic racist from the 1920s. It doesn't matter if you're trying to be offensive or not, what matters is how you respond when you're called out on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are you just going to ignore the <b>extreme xenophobia</b> of the Chinese and Japanese pantheons that continues to exist to this day?<br /> <br /> Or the caste system of Hinduism? Because that sounds a hell of a lot like Lovecraft's arguments in favor of class warfare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-13-2019, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T19:40:01-08:00","id":1280595,"title":"","content":"At least on the last one several of the Hindu gods are outright defiant of the caste system. It\u2019s apparently in a lot of their religious texts which makes a lot of the caste system a human thing. <br /> <br /> As to others being popular and sociologically impactful is not the only thing that goes into religion. Yeah sure there\u2019s lots of things inspired by Lovecraft there\u2019s lots of comic books too but Marvel is not a religion. Disney is not a religion. The House of Windsor is not a religion. The NFL is not a religion.<br /> <br /> Also as to the \u201ctrack record of these religions\u201d People do horrible things. They choose to do those horrible things. Blaming religion, money, or anything else is passing the buck in a way I do not accept. Without religion horrible things would still happen. It\u2019s a non-entity as far as people doing horrible things and trying to lay blame on it is trying to shift responsibility away from ourselves. We do the horrible things. We do the good things. Regardless of whether you\u2019re religious or not the responsibility is on us not the religion. <br /> <br /> If a religious leader uses propaganda and biased interpretations of a thing to rouse violence that\u2019s on him not the religion. If the mob he rouses kills or otherwise harms someone they are to blame. They may feel justified by some guy suggesting that they are asked to do this but they still make the decision in the end. <br /> <br /> \u201cPower corrupts\u201d \u201cmoney changes people\u201d \u201creligion chains us down\u201d<br /> <br /> These are all statements meant to excuse our decisions or those of other people to take actions we know to be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","user":"Thrythlind","date":". 01-13-2019, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T19:59:36-08:00","id":1280598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280594#post1280594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And as I said, the only difference between Lovecraft and the other religions is time. The actual bible wasn't written and codified until 30 years after Jesus' death. The idea of cosmic horror and us living in a cold, uncaring universe is becoming increasingly more prevalent over the years. Two of the most popular cartoons in recent history (Rick and Morty, and Bojack Horseman) heavily revolve around these concepts as the focus of their series.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be able to make that comparison with the TDD, but none of the other pantheons were created as intentional fiction and then later people started believing them. So no - the difference isn't just time.<br /> <br /> Both of those are shows more about specific characters' disfunction than any actual horror at cosmic uncaringness. That's more how the awful leads project and make excuses for themselves. But, to the extent they are about that - Bojack is primarily influenced by Pascal and Sartre. While Rick &amp; Morty has less thought put into its philosophical viewpoint by comparison, it definitely isn't Lovecraftian, because there's no horror at how unknowable and alien the universe is. That's kid stuff to a mind like Rick's. You can't get more anti-Lovecraftian than a great mind kicking the universe's ass. There is absolutely nihilism underlying the show and an existentialist struggle against it, mostly via the idea that infinite realities make everything meaningless as there's always another universe where any given tragedy didn't happen, or where some tragedy you prevented did, etc etc - but again, that's not what Lovecraft was talking about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not arguing against the product - for one reason because the things Neall has mentioned on the discord have made it clear the book's presenting a very distinct Shard and they're well aware that the Mythos can't be just one factor in the World - if it's in there, you're playing Lovecraft-Scion. That corralling of the subject matter and making clear it's distinct from the World, not just an optional insert, makes me a lot more comfortable with the premise of the book. But conflating the fiction of the Mythos with real religion is just... completely wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-13-2019, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T20:54:20-08:00","id":1280608,"title":"","content":"And beyond all the other bullcrap that comes with Lovecraft's works (which y'know, keep those in mind) the nihilistic bullshit dread of the 'Mythos' falls apart when introduced to the Mainline Scion, where other Gods are NOT fake.<br /> <br /> Why fear Hastur when Thor exists and can bring the might of Mjolnir?<br /> <br /> Why dread the Black Goat when Kali can just devour it and its countless young?<br /> <br /> Why fear the waking of Azathoth trying to unmake the World when the Netjer literally keep the sun safe from a giant cosmic serpent every night? Or the Teotl, who fight a war against the demons of the night to keep the World safe?<br /> <br /> This is the World of Scion. The Gods are real, and many of them are going to bat for humanity. Fear not: You are not alone.<br /> <br /> That, ultimately, is why Cthulhu doesn't work in mainline Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T21:20:30-08:00","id":1280615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280608#post1280608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And beyond all the other bullcrap that comes with Lovecraft's works (which y'know, keep those in mind) the nihilistic bullshit dread of the 'Mythos' falls apart when introduced to the Mainline Scion, where other Gods are NOT fake.<br /> <br /> Why fear Hastur when Thor exists and can bring the might of Mjolnir?<br /> <br /> Why dread the Black Goat when Kali can just devour it and its countless young?<br /> <br /> Why fear the waking of Azathoth trying to unmake the World when the Netjer literally keep the sun safe from a giant cosmic serpent every night? Or the Teotl, who fight a war against the demons of the night to keep the World safe?<br /> <br /> This is the World of Scion. The Gods are real, and many of them are going to bat for humanity. Fear not: You are not alone.<br /> <br /> That, ultimately, is why Cthulhu doesn't work in mainline Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The reason why Shub-Niggurath is terrifying is because she was supposed to represent that there is nothing sacred, or miraculous about life. The gods themselves were born out of the chaos that is Azathoth's madness. A happy little accident, nothing more. And if the creation of the gods was the result of pure, random chance, then the creation of mortal life must be equally accidental, if not more so.<br /> <br /> <br /> Protecting <b>A</b> star from a snake and preventing the <b>entire universe</b> from exploding are two entirely different scales of threat. How about the fact that even the cosmic horrors themselves are actively trying to keep Azathoth asleep? I'm sure that speaks volumes about the level of danger he poses.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Thor bringing the might of Mjolnir, remember that Thor is destined to die at the fangs of a snake who's big enough to wrap around the earth twice. But guess how many earths can fit inside our sun? <b>1,300,000.</b> By comparison, Thor's death seems rather pathetic, wouldn't you say?<br /> <br /> <br /> And on the subject of the Teotl, keep in mind that they failed like 4 or 5 times, before finally managing to create the world we live in now...<br /> <br /> <br /> If Scion was a game about portraying how great humanity is, then it would be a game that focuses on playing a human. Not somebody who is on the path to literal godhood and will become so powerful by the time they reach Demigod status, that nothing short of a military operation would be able to threaten them.<br /> <br /> And in 2nd edition, you don't even have to be a human Scion, anymore! You can play a giant, a kitsune, a centaur, a satyr, a tengu, or whatever the heck you want!<br /> <br /> Additionally, you don't necessarily have to side with the Gods, either. You can play a Scion who goes on to become a Titan! So saying that the Old Gods don't mesh with Scion because they don't care about humanity is only applicable to 1st edition. When it comes to 2nd edition, there's plenty of wiggle room that you can slip them in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T21:36:35-08:00","id":1280616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280615#post1280615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Protecting <b>A</b> star from a snake and preventing the <b>entire universe</b> from exploding are two entirely different scales of threat. How about the fact that even the cosmic horrors themselves are actively trying to keep Azathoth asleep? I'm sure that speaks volumes about the level of danger he poses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you might be misinformed, if Ra blinks reality ends. The Netjer defend the sun to the death because if the sun goes out with the death of Ra, everything that ever has been, or is never has. It all returns to nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 01-14-2019, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T21:46:53-08:00","id":1280617,"title":"","content":"And basing measurements of Jormungandr on Earth presumes that Midgard is limited to Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T22:00:05-08:00","id":1280625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thrythlind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280617#post1280617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And basing measurements of Jormungandr on Earth presumes that Midgard is limited to Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, he's supposed to be hiding under our sea, so it makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T22:08:37-08:00","id":1280627,"title":"","content":"The sea can also refer to the cosmos and does in a many mythologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T22:21:35-08:00","id":1280631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280594#post1280594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as I said, the only difference between Lovecraft and the other religions is time.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">There is so much wrong with this statement I don\u2019t even know where to begin. Suffice it to say, this is extremely disrespectful to every religion, and respect is rules 1 and 2 on these forums. Don\u2019t post in this thread again.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T22:49:17-08:00","id":1280637,"title":"","content":"Also, just gonna add for the record - a big part of the horror of Lovecraft is the context of the time it was written in. When Lovecraft was writing about the impossible vastness of the cosmos to try to scare people, common wisdom was that science was pretty close to done. People were genuinely pretty sure that we\u2019d learned pretty much everything there was to learn, and that we\u2019d solve the last few remaining questions within a generation or so.<br /> <br /> Now, I teach fucking 4-year-olds about the incomprehensible size of the universe in a 30-minute Planetarium show on a daily basis. The idea that we\u2019re tiny and insignificant was a big, scary deal in the 30s. It\u2019s common knowledge now. Contrary to being on its way to becoming a religion, the Cthulhu mythos is a pop cultural touchstone at best, and a played-out meme at worst. Nihlism isn\u2019t a revelation any more, it\u2019s the subject of animated sit-coms. That\u2019s as far from religious significance as you can get. Lovecraftian horror is not awe-inspiring any more, it\u2019s not even scary any more, it\u2019s a literal joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-13T23:57:02-08:00","id":1280645,"title":"","content":"Game's tagline is 'Every Myth is True... only if they are not Scientologist or Lovecraft fan'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But the <b>Scion Mythos</b> being massive Shard just solves all the gameline problems with product. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-14-2019, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T01:46:57-08:00","id":1280650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280645#post1280645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Game's tagline is 'Every Myth is True... only if they are not Scientologist or Lovecraft fan'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That was not what was said here. Scientologist belief would not be true because there is no shard to reality that connects the belief to reality. There is no real bases for anything that is taught in Scientology, as far as I know, and the history presented there is... out there, to put it mildly. Scion 2ed has been presented that all myth must have a bases to reality: Thor might have been a guy who, one day, hit a tree with a hammer and that tree was hit a by a lightning, give a few centuries, he throws his hammer and summons the lightning. Susano-o might have been a lord of a land with a castle near the sea, in which during high waters, the waters flooded around the castle, give a few centuries, his castle is under the sea and he is the Sea lord. Scientology has none. It didnt develop, one myth at the time, and then got together forming an intricate tapestry of tales. A guy wrote about it, from no basis but his own creative mind, and got luck.<br /> (Again, as far as I know. If there is any Scientologist here, I would love to talk to you and apologize if you felt offended with my comment, and maybe have a nice discussion about the topic, if you feel like it.)<br /> <br /> Scam religions also exist in the World.<br /> <br /> Also, you said it right, Lovecraftian fan. Fan. Not worshiper. Fan. And even if there were worshipers, again, the Mythos have no bases. It is a creation of fiction, by a very creative and incredible eloquent mind. Lovecraft didnt saw a squid in a beach, and while flooping it captured a seagull and then, a few centuries later, a giant squid/dragon/human/weirdness monster lived in a sunk city into the ocean. He probably saw a squid at some point, which he probably feared as I have read that he was sea-phobic, and used that to model the creature in his story. Not the same thing.<br /> <br /> All Myths are true, not all stories are true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12934,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","user":"Manbat","date":". 01-14-2019, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T02:42:52-08:00","id":1280655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280645#post1280645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Game's tagline is 'Every Myth is True... only if they are not Scientologist or Lovecraft fan'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay seriously cut the ego, buddy. You're not a third as clever as you think you are. Lovecraft isn't myth, it's the paranoid ramblings of a thoroughly garbage human being who wrote a book about horrifying human-fish hybrids after finding out he has Welsh ancestry. Charlaquin said it best: The Mythos isn't a religion, it's a joke that's no longer funny. It's nowhere near as deep as I've seen some people claim it is.<br /> <br /> I doubt that there will be more Scion: Mythos products. Because it's not like there's a huge number of Elder Gods in the Mythos. You don't really need more than one book, most likely. And those who want their Scion Cthulhu, sure, sounds like you'll have it. As its own thing, kept far away from Mainline Scion, which is good, as I'd prefer to keep it as far away from mainline Scion as possible.<br /> <br /> (Seriously though, They Came From Beneath The Sea would probably be a better Storypath system to use as a base for Stories of the Cthulhu Mythos.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T05:37:29-08:00","id":1280675,"title":"","content":"Frankly speaking, Scientology has more claim to exist as a divine faith in Scion than Lovecraft does - not a ton more, but more - on the basis that actual, real humans are devout Scientologists - indeed, some without actually being part of the whole organizing group behind mainstream Scientology.<br /> <br /> The Mythos is not a religion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T10:39:18-08:00","id":1280706,"title":"","content":"Damn timezones... I wish I could have posted this earlier... nevertheless, someone may find the general info useful for their games <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If we're talking Scale, the entire manifest Universe that Azathoth apparently created is merely three of the Deva's fourteen Realms... there's another eleven that are huge, multiple of them being literally as large as you need it to be, such as the realm of the Asura Architect Maya. And then you have Naraka, which is infinitely spreading in all directions.<br /> <br /> All these together make up a single Samsara, ruled over by Brahma Vishnu and Shiva. They arise from the Eternal Infinite Godhead and at the end of their lifetimes return to it... do you know how long that lifetime is? On the order of 300 trillion years.<br /> <br /> But wait, it gets better... this is merely a single Samsara... a million million Samsaras, each with their own Brahma Vishnu and Shiva, arise from the Godhead... when the three from our universe go to meet their maker (in this story the Goddess Durga) they see an infinite number of Samsara in a single one of her toenails, each of which has it's own version of themselves.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Azathoth is starting to look a little pathetic.<br /> <br /> If one were to look on the other hand at the embodiment of space-time that is Yog-Sototh, let me merely quote this hymn:<br /> <br /> &quot;That which impels and devours (kalana) all things is Kala (Time)... He who impels and devours Kala, is MahaKala (Great Time) Shiva... and She who impels and devours MahaKala, is Adya Kali (Primordial Kali)&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, that's him had for breakfast. All the other Mythos beings go down from there.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk Cosmic Incomprehensible Gods, the Deva are way ahead of Lovecraft...<br /> <br /> &quot;Such was the massive form that the best of gods beheld,<br /> With its thousands of blazing rays, licking with its tongue,<br /> Producing horrible crunching sounds with its teeth, spewing fire from its eyes, Holding various weapons, heroic in stature, making mush of sages and warriors for its food.<br /> It had a thousand heads and eyes, and a thousand feet as well, Resembling millions of suns, radiant like millions of lightning streaks.<br /> That fearful, horrific form, terrifying to heart and eye, All the gods beheld and wailed, &quot;Woe unto us, woe!&quot;<br /> With trembling hearts, they swooned helplessly. Even the thought, &quot;This is the World Mother,&quot; escaped them.<br /> Then the Vedas, stationed on the four sides of the Great Ruling Goddess, With much effort awakened the unconscious gods from their swoon.&quot;<br /> <br /> About the only real difference here (other than the Mythos beings being fairly small fish in comparison) is that the Deva actually give a shit about mortals. Since, surprise, not all Gods are dicks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T10:41:44-08:00","id":1280707,"title":"","content":"I mean, the entire Azathoth issue can be handled by one guy. Hypnos, comma, the literal anthropomorphic personification of Sleep. He doesn't even have to break a sweat.<br /> <br /> And he's not even very important, certainly not compared to all these folks that've been mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T12:00:01-08:00","id":1280717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorsRattus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280707#post1280707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the entire Azathoth issue can be handled by one guy. Hypnos, comma, the literal anthropomorphic personification of Sleep. He doesn't even have to break a sweat.<br /> <br /> And he's not even very important, certainly not compared to all these folks that've been mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... crammed into Scion terminology (which i\u2019m not saying works well, but if we\u2019re doing this thought exercise, then fine let\u2019s do it) Azathoth would be a Primordail, so he probably has Scale on Hypnos. Not saying Hypnos couldn\u2019t handle it, but he might need to actually TRY and break a sweat in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T12:26:05-08:00","id":1280725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280706#post1280706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn timezones... I wish I could have posted this earlier... nevertheless, someone may find the general info useful for their games <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If we're talking Scale, the entire manifest Universe that Azathoth apparently created is merely three of the Deva's fourteen Realms... there's another eleven that are huge, multiple of them being literally as large as you need it to be, such as the realm of the Asura Architect Maya. And then you have Naraka, which is infinitely spreading in all directions.<br /> <br /> All these together make up a single Samsara, ruled over by Brahma Vishnu and Shiva. They arise from the Eternal Infinite Godhead and at the end of their lifetimes return to it... do you know how long that lifetime is? On the order of 300 trillion years.<br /> <br /> But wait, it gets better... this is merely a single Samsara... a million million Samsaras, each with their own Brahma Vishnu and Shiva, arise from the Godhead... when the three from our universe go to meet their maker (in this story the Goddess Durga) they see an infinite number of Samsara in a single one of her toenails, each of which has it's own version of themselves.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Azathoth is starting to look a little pathetic.<br /> <br /> If one were to look on the other hand at the embodiment of space-time that is Yog-Sototh, let me merely quote this hymn:<br /> <br /> &quot;That which impels and devours (kalana) all things is Kala (Time)... He who impels and devours Kala, is MahaKala (Great Time) Shiva... and She who impels and devours MahaKala, is Adya Kali (Primordial Kali)&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, that's him had for breakfast. All the other Mythos beings go down from there.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk Cosmic Incomprehensible Gods, the Deva are way ahead of Lovecraft...<br /> <br /> &quot;Such was the massive form that the best of gods beheld,<br /> With its thousands of blazing rays, licking with its tongue,<br /> Producing horrible crunching sounds with its teeth, spewing fire from its eyes, Holding various weapons, heroic in stature, making mush of sages and warriors for its food.<br /> It had a thousand heads and eyes, and a thousand feet as well, Resembling millions of suns, radiant like millions of lightning streaks.<br /> That fearful, horrific form, terrifying to heart and eye, All the gods beheld and wailed, &quot;Woe unto us, woe!&quot;<br /> With trembling hearts, they swooned helplessly. Even the thought, &quot;This is the World Mother,&quot; escaped them.<br /> Then the Vedas, stationed on the four sides of the Great Ruling Goddess, With much effort awakened the unconscious gods from their swoon.&quot;<br /> <br /> About the only real difference here (other than the Mythos beings being fairly small fish in comparison) is that the Deva actually give a shit about mortals. Since, surprise, not all Gods are dicks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>India: This being is incomprhensible because it is a thousand thousand things at once, it's body being made of all the other gods, thus containing the whole universe.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft: This being is incomprehensible because it's head is a squid. I am afraid of sea food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T13:51:36-08:00","id":1280741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280717#post1280717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well... crammed into Scion terminology (which i\u2019m not saying works well, but if we\u2019re doing this thought exercise, then fine let\u2019s do it) Azathoth would be a Primordail, so he probably has Scale on Hypnos. Not saying Hypnos couldn\u2019t handle it, but he might need to actually TRY and break a sweat in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Azathoth may have Scale on Hypnos, but Primordials and Gods operate on the same Tier. So yeah, Hypnos could totally work his magic on Azathoth","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T14:04:28-08:00","id":1280749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280741#post1280741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Azathoth may have Scale on Hypnos, but Primordials and Gods operate on the same Tier. So yeah, Hypnos could totally work his magic on Azathoth</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure he can invoke a title to match scale on that matter too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T14:25:44-08:00","id":1280754,"title":"","content":"As a fanatic of both Lovecraftian horror and mythology alike there's a lot of frankly ignorant comments about both in this thread and I'm awfully disappointed to see that reaction. <br /> <br /> We know so little about what this supplement actually entails, let alone how it will reconcile the disparate heroic themes of Scion and the coldly materialist themes of Lovecraft ( I don't find Lovecraft's work to be strictly nihilistic but that's a schematic argument for another day) together. But I will say I trust the devs on this book, I get the sense that this will be a full on conversion on running Scion as a cosmic horror game and not just a tacked on Great Old One pantheon write up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T14:33:05-08:00","id":1280763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280754#post1280754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a fanatic of both Lovecraftian horror and mythology alike there's a lot of frankly ignorant comments about both in this thread and I'm awfully disappointed to see that reaction. <br /> <br /> We know so little about what this supplement actually entails, let alone how it will reconcile the disparate heroic themes of Scion and the coldly materialist themes of Lovecraft ( I don't find Lovecraft's work to be strictly nihilistic but that's a schematic argument for another day) together. But I will say I trust the devs on this book, I get the sense that this will be a full on conversion on running Scion as a cosmic horror game and not just a tacked on Great Old One pantheon write up.</div> </div> </div> </div>We know from Discord comments that the product won't take place in the World as shown in the Origin and Hero books, that's enough for me to ignore it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T20:04:31-08:00","id":1280816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280754#post1280754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a fanatic of both Lovecraftian horror and mythology alike there's a lot of frankly ignorant comments about both in this thread and I'm awfully disappointed to see that reaction. <br /> <br /> We know so little about what this supplement actually entails, let alone how it will reconcile the disparate heroic themes of Scion and the coldly materialist themes of Lovecraft ( I don't find Lovecraft's work to be strictly nihilistic but that's a schematic argument for another day) together. But I will say I trust the devs on this book, I get the sense that this will be a full on conversion on running Scion as a cosmic horror game and not just a tacked on Great Old One pantheon write up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lovecraft is one of the few writers commonly called nihilistic who actually DOES deserve the label, as that\u2019s the entire hook of the horror - the terror at one\u2019s own insignificance before the unknowable vastness of the universe that must be ignored to survive. He deserves the label in that regard far more than the existentialists it gets wrongly applied to like Nietzsche or Sartre.<br /> <br /> Now one can argue the nihilism of his work is undercut by those forces of civilization he does imply are worth struggling to preserve, but as said forces amount to \u201cthe racial purity of white New Englanders\u201d and \u201cthe social hierarchy where white New Englanders are at the top and everyone else knows their place serving them\u201d I prefer to focus on the nihilism as the positive aspect of the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-14-2019, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T01:51:55-08:00","id":1280858,"title":"","content":"It is a supplement book. You do not have to buy it, let alone use it<br /> <br /> I hope it is a Titan pantheon book (the Great Olds Ones don't really fit anything else with the exception of that one mad primordial). It might also be an alternative setting. The GOO don't exactly play well with other divine entities. Regardless, we can use it as such.<br /> <br /> The source material has several issues arising from the author's bigotry. I wonder if that will carry on into the flaws of the pantheon.<br /> <br /> To the best of my knowledge, no one in this our world worshiped these guys to any serious degree. I don't see that overly changing in the World.<br /> <br /> I understand that there are many real world mythologies full of awesome that have not been brought into Scion yet. I also understand that we want them to be well researched and well written by those who understand them. To this end, Lovecraft's works of fiction are a low hanging fruit of easy to access English language primary source materials. Not exactly going to blame them when they still are so busy. Certainly, I see Demigod taking a lot of the trusted talent on that front.<br /> <br /> Can we just try and enjoy the news for what it is? Scion is not a limited line and is getting more support from the home office before it is released to the GP! That is fantastic. Two supplements (Mythos &amp; Dragons), not counting the Companion (Mysteries) before the first two Core books are out while the third is being written. That is a lot rather quickly. We aren't being forgotten. We still have those other ideas they bandied around too. Scion: Sorcerers and the Once and Future King are unlikely to have been forgotten even if they aren't up next. Besides Mythos andbDragons haven't been outlined yet, let alone assigned authors. Give them time.<br /> <br /> They might actually know what they are doing. It is not a big stretch.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T02:23:48-08:00","id":1280863,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a> really wrote all I think about Scion Mythos supplement - best written, mate!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T04:43:32-08:00","id":1280874,"title":"","content":"To be clear, I would have no issue with Onyx Path doing a cthulhu Storypath game....and with what Neall has said indicating that Scion cthulhu is going to be very not canon and very optional off in its own thing, I'm okay with that....what we had issue with was a game that was advertising its respect to cultures and religions and doing appropriate research to treat things well with devoting time and manpower from the team toward building a supplement for a something that was very disrespectful of most cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T04:43:47-08:00","id":1280875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280741#post1280741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Azathoth may have Scale on Hypnos, but Primordials and Gods operate on the same Tier. So yeah, Hypnos could totally work his magic on Azathoth</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they change that? Because I could have sworn Titans had Scale on Gods in their wheelhouse, at least in the early preview material. Since Primodrial Emanations can easily pass as Titans (to the point of making the latter uncomfortable) I think Primordials might be bigger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T05:47:14-08:00","id":1280882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280655#post1280655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay seriously cut the ego, buddy. You're not a third as clever as you think you are. Lovecraft isn't myth, it's the paranoid ramblings of a thoroughly garbage human being who wrote a book about horrifying human-fish hybrids after finding out he has Welsh ancestry. Charlaquin said it best: The Mythos isn't a religion, it's a joke that's no longer funny. It's nowhere near as deep as I've seen some people claim it is.<br /> <br /> I doubt that there will be more Scion: Mythos products. Because it's not like there's a huge number of Elder Gods in the Mythos. You don't really need more than one book, most likely. And those who want their Scion Cthulhu, sure, sounds like you'll have it. As its own thing, kept far away from Mainline Scion, which is good, as I'd prefer to keep it as far away from mainline Scion as possible.<br /> <br /> (Seriously though, They Came From Beneath The Sea would probably be a better Storypath system to use as a base for Stories of the Cthulhu Mythos.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mythos isn't even Lovecraft, it's Chaosium(primarily). Also learn to talk a bit nicer to people could you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 01-15-2019, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T07:01:52-08:00","id":1280890,"title":"","content":"Chaosium is the gaming company that produces the rpg &quot;The Call of Cthulhu.&quot; They didn't create the Mythos. It was created by the author H.P. Lovecraft back in the 1920's in a series of short stories, and is now in the public domain (which means anyone can use it in their stories movies, or games free of charge).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T07:11:27-08:00","id":1280894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280890#post1280890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chaosium is the gaming company that produces the rpg &quot;The Call of Cthulhu.&quot; They didn't create the Mythos. It was created by the author H.P. Lovecraft back in the 1920's in a series of short stories, and is now in the public domain (which means anyone can use it in their stories movies, or games free of charge).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that he never did. Lovecraft never created a coherent &quot;mythos&quot; and told his frequent writer pen pals he had later in his life to use what they wanted. There was never anything codified and a lot of what we think of nowadays as the mythos is derived from things Chaosium(not JUST them, in case someone would like to trot out that strawman) later injected and intimated. It was never his real intention to create such a thing and a great deal of what pop culture thinks of the Mythos came after.<br /> <br /> Given the immense amount of saturation of Lovecraft's influences in film and literature this really shouldn't be a surprise to anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 01-15-2019, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T08:03:20-08:00","id":1280901,"title":"","content":"I see you've edited your post to clarify. What I got from the original was that you thought that Chaosium came up the original elements of the Mythos, and I was intending to point out that H.P. Lovecraft - not the esteemed gaming company - invented many of the elements associated with the &quot;Mythos&quot; today [though many other authors have expanded and contributed]. No more, no less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T08:14:51-08:00","id":1280902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280901#post1280901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see you've edited your post to clarify. What I got from the original was that you thought that Chaosium came up the original elements of the Mythos, and I was intending to point out that H.P. Lovecraft - not the esteemed gaming company - invented many of the elements associated with the &quot;Mythos&quot; today [though many other authors have expanded and contributed]. No more, no less.</div> </div> </div> </div>In and of itself, that doesn't mean very much. Particularly in light of the way that Lovecraft has been adopted and influences felt in the intervening time. Also I wasn't clarifying, I was hedging my bets against people attempting to make bad faith arguments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T08:31:53-08:00","id":1280908,"title":"","content":"I haven't gotten a chance to read Harlem Unbound yet, but the consensus is Spivey handled the Cthulhu Mythos in 1920's Harlem very deftly. I would expect similar care to be taken here with regards to the Mythos and race. As for putting the Mythos on par with real world religions, we don't know how it's going to be presented yet. So, I'm willing to give them a chance. We'll see what they do with it. Hopefully they take people's concerns to heart and avoid any pitfalls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T10:30:47-08:00","id":1280932,"title":"","content":"Why is it that no-one seems capable any more of just saying, &quot;cool, I see what you meant, no worries&quot;, and moving on, without defending their position and digging in, when all that was intended was a well-meant (if ultimately unneeded) clarification of a perceived mistake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T12:41:16-08:00","id":1280958,"title":"","content":"While I would never use Lovecraft's specific creations in my Scion game, I admit there are some uses for this book I think I can harvest if it's done well. In the American Gods inspired Shard i'm tinkering with, I'm thinking of using original &quot;Cosmic Horror&quot; homages as the Titans of my &quot;Modern Gods&quot; pantheon - reflecting the nihilistic horror of a material universe, while the gods of the pantheon represent the various worldly things that people turn to hold despair at bay. A good tentacly/madnessy PSP would be helpful for stealing for said original Cosmic Horror Titans' brood and cultists.<br /> <br /> (Note: this is specifically a Shard. A &quot;Modern Gods&quot; Pantheon doesn't work in the World, because an assumption of the setting is that the &quot;Old Gods&quot; have kept up. They aren't at odds with modernity, they encompass it in their respective divine roles and patronages. This is a very different setting in both tone, setting assumptions, and even some mechanics)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-15-2019, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T18:40:30-08:00","id":1281023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280763#post1280763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We know from Discord comments that the product won't take place in the World as shown in the Origin and Hero books, that's enough for me to ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The World is immensely mutable and customizeable by players and Storyguides, by design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T18:55:52-08:00","id":1281027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1281023#post1281023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The World is immensely mutable and customizeable by players and Storyguides, by design.</div> </div> </div> </div>How can a setting though in which souls move to afterlives of legend, and there are higher powers that care about humans or at least human civilization, support an additional cosmology and beings who thematically hinge on the horror of finite materialism in an alien uncaring universe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T02:54:21-08:00","id":1281066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1281027#post1281027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How can a setting though in which souls move to afterlives of legend, and there are higher powers that care about humans or at least human civilization, support an additional cosmology and beings who thematically hinge on the horror of finite materialism in an alien uncaring universe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Mythos Pantheon wants to destroy the afterlives too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T02:59:36-08:00","id":1281067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1281066#post1281066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the Mythos Pantheon wants to destroy the afterlives too?</div> </div> </div> </div>In which case, the question inevitably arises, why haven't the other Pantheons had them for breakfast yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 01-16-2019, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T07:42:51-08:00","id":1281092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1281067#post1281067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In which case, the question inevitably arises, why haven't the other Pantheons had them for breakfast yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a question only a suppliment that &quot;takes the Eldritch beings of the <b>Cthulhu Mythos</b> and tackles how to deal with them, and the baggage they bring, as a <b>Scion </b>game&quot; could be able to answer. It's just more options. Im intrigued to see how it all works out but I think it's too soon to really theorize concrete answers on the direction it's going to take. Whichever way it does go the vailidity and usefullness of the product will hinge on how well they support and structure it's inclusion. What I do know is my friend who is a massive lovecraft fan shit himself with excitement when he heard Scion was trying to find a way to properly include them in an official way.<br /> <br /> EDIT: My only concern is I hope whatever they do with Mythos and Dragon they make sure it supports the full advancement of Dragons and Mythos from Origin through God. Which means I hope they stay in development until after Scion: God is complete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 01-16-2019, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T08:24:59-08:00","id":1281103,"title":"","content":"How about just focus on completing the indexing for Hero and Origin (which seems to be taking an eon in itself) and getting Demigod, God and the Companion out before you guys decide to delve into weird stuff. <br /> <br /> Adding the Cthulhu Mythos to Scion is possible the worst idea I can think of. The reasons are varied and have been mentioned by other members.<br /> <br /> If you were adamant about making something that fits scion why not an ancient World setting. The Dawn of the gods? Ancient Greece, Imperial Japan, Warring States China, India... explaining Dharka... even Ancient Sweden ect...<br /> <br /> But Cthulhu? Really?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T08:47:34-08:00","id":1281107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1281066#post1281066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the Mythos Pantheon wants to destroy the afterlives too?</div> </div> </div> </div>That implies way more caring about humanity that representations of an alien, cold, meaningless universe should be doing.<br /> <br /> The Outer Gods and Great Old Ones aren\u2019t malicious. They DON\u2019T CARE. That\u2019s the entire point.<br /> <br /> In a setting with higher powers that do care about humanity, you\u2019ve defeated the entire horror hook the Mythos represents. What\u2019s the point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T08:56:44-08:00","id":1281109,"title":"","content":"Is there a reason that they have to suddenly care just because they are in the Scion world? Their scions could be created/born and experience their awakenings in very different ways due to their distance and lack of care. Also, them being distant doesn't mean their influence has to be distant or weak as well. They could be justified as being even stronger than gods but so remote and uncaring that they don't flip the war and setting on its head. Having a Scion of one of them in the same party as a Scion of Thor is going to be very distinct and different and the interactions between those characters could be really awesome. The cultures of their origins would vary more wildly than any two other pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 01-16-2019, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T09:15:28-08:00","id":1281113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1281109#post1281109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a reason that they have to suddenly care just because they are in the Scion world? Their scions could be created/born and experience their awakenings in very different ways due to their distance and lack of care. Also, them being distant doesn't mean their influence has to be distant or weak as well. They could be justified as being even stronger than gods but so remote and uncaring that they don't flip the war and setting on its head. Having a Scion of one of them in the same party as a Scion of Thor is going to be very distinct and different and the interactions between those characters could be really awesome. The cultures of their origins would vary more wildly than any two other pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s no point to their presence if the universe cares. The point of the Mythos is that the universe is cold and alien and unknowable and your existence is meaningless. If that\u2019s not the case in the setting what\u2019s the point? Tentacles are scary?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T09:44:25-08:00","id":1281118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1281113#post1281113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There\u2019s no point to their presence if the universe cares. The point of the Mythos is that the universe is cold and alien and unknowable and your existence is meaningless. If that\u2019s not the case in the setting what\u2019s the point? Tentacles are scary?</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I may have gotten a bit heated earlier in the thread, sleeping on it a bit may have made me realize something.<br /> <br /> I really don't find the thematic horror of the Cthulhu Mythos that scary. Like, to me, I don't find Cthulhu scary in any sense beyond 'Big monster that may want to eat me', and in that sense it's no scarier to me than say, Godzilla.<br /> <br /> If the universe is big and we're that insignificant and in the cosmic scale nothing we do matters... Well, I don't find that scary. Or depressing, really. Because a short way for me to answer the question of &quot;What's the point if eventually things give way to entropy, life is an accident, and most of us will die in a cosmic instant&quot; is &quot;... I like pizza&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, sounds silly, but it's a short way to describe my feelings. Pizza's great. So's cake, spaghetti, and a good hearty chicken soup.<br /> <br /> Does any of this matter on a cosmic scale? Nope, not in the least. But I won't live on a cosmic timeline. I don't see the point in worrying about that. I don't even find any kind of dread in being more than an okay everyman in our world in my lifetime. I just try to do right, maybe make some connections so that people will miss me when I die, do my best to try and make this world a bit better than when I came into it.<br /> <br /> My horror is much more personal. Show me a grave with my name on it, obviously untended, and nobody ever stops by. A funeral that nobody went to because I managed to drive off everybody I knew in life. That, to me, is a million times more horrifying than the implication that I'm not the most important thing in the universe. That's so much more emotionally devastating than telling me that life is nothing more than an accident with no greater plan.<br /> <br /> Ugh, I may have had a point somewhere. Mostly I'll say to any fans of the Cthulhu Mythos I may have insulted... I'm sorry, I didn't mean to insult you or try and say you're a bad person if you like it.<br /> <br /> I still don't think it fits in with mainline Scion and think that it's best done as a separate continuity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T10:39:59-08:00","id":1281128,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7AwdYpkngRk\" target=\"_blank\">Mid-Winter interview with Neall points ( at 2:40) that <b>Scion: Masks of Mythos</b> will be centered on Scions of Old Ones.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T11:10:20-08:00","id":1281135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1281128#post1281128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7AwdYpkngRk\" target=\"_blank\">Mid-Winter interview with Neall points ( at 2:40) that <b>Scion: Masks of Mythos</b> will be centered on Scions of Old Ones.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And he says it's an alternate setting, if that allays anyone's fears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T12:21:23-08:00","id":1281152,"title":"","content":"I will simply be exercising my right to not support the KS or buy the supplement - it just doesn't work for me. YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T12:24:54-08:00","id":1281153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1281135#post1281135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And he says it's an alternate setting, if that allays anyone's fears.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I'm down for it as an alternate setting. Wouldn't use it straight, but I'll harvest it like crazy. It just makes no sense to me at all as something to insert alongside pantheons of human religion as real powers because that thematically defeats the point of the Mythos (by comparison, my American Gods homage Shard, which is more thematically existentialist and has Cosmic Horrors as Titans, the &quot;Old Gods&quot; only appear in the form of Incarnate Player Characters at Hero level. There are no &quot;higher powers&quot;, because it's a very different cosmology from the World, that ala American Gods plays off the creative power of human belief rather than metaphysical truths).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T19:30:52-08:00","id":1281736,"title":"","content":"Personally I love the idea of Mythos book for Scion. Then again my 1st ed Scion games never had more than one Panth\u00e9on in existence at a time. Why? Because for me it makes no sense to have several omnipotent gods of the same thing. If we have one sun god that matters but if we have 5 sun gods non of them matter since each could undo what any other tried to do with the sun. Naturally YMMV but for me having all religions be right and true disrespects each of those religions just as much as having none of them be true or having fictional Panth\u00e9ons around. Again these are just my personal opinions but I immensly disliked the fictional Panth\u00e9ons of 1st ed but Chtulhu Mythos I can work with.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though we will see if the Masks of Mythos or Scion: Dragons are good supplements once they get into the actual writing and we know a bit more about them than just their titles. No reason to get so angry about them especially since they are worked by different teams than those focusing on furthering Scion core books.<br /> <br /> We all like different things. I like to play like only the Panth\u00e9on that is real and true is the one the current game is about but I get why others like the idea of playing with mixed Panth\u00e9ons. I am interested in Mythos through the lens of Scion but I get it is not for everyone. So the best thing that can happen is that they write several books about different subjects and we as consumers buy the books that interest us. No harm no foul and each of us gets some nice things from the game we all love.<br /> <br /> So how about we chill and wait for them to write the books first before shooting them down, the authors may surprise us pleasantly after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T19:55:20-08:00","id":1281738,"title":"","content":"Scion includes an element where each Creation Myth gets retroactively applied to the World, and so in a sense they're all true. I could see something similar applying to a Mythos-derived Pantheon, should you want to mix it with other Pantheons. <br /> <br /> Still, I like that it's \u201cofficially unofficial\u201d, highlighting that you don't have to use it if you don't want to (as if you ever do, for <i>anything</i> in Scion). <br /> <br /> Several posters have said that Lovecraft's creations don't really fit the Scion mold. That's fine by me; I would be thrilled if the Old Ones turned out to be \u201cin the same Tier as Gods, Titans, and Primordials, but without actually being Gods, Titans, or Primordials\u201d. That is, if they don't fit the mold, have them break it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T23:06:27-08:00","id":1281752,"title":"","content":"And the teaser in that video mentioned that there'll be rules for being descended from the Old Ones. Which, alright, fair, that's a spin that Scion would manage, mechanically.<br /> <br /> I admit I've cooled somewhat on the Mythos having its own shard. Still probably won't buy it buy there ya go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 01-20-2019, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T00:26:43-08:00","id":1281753,"title":"","content":"Without Spivey now confirmed as full blown book developer for MotM, I am much more optimistic about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T06:38:14-08:00","id":1281771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280608#post1280608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why fear Hastur when Thor exists and can bring the might of Mjolnir?<br /> <br /> Why dread the Black Goat when Kali can just devour it and its countless young?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think the idea of Thor punching Cthulhu in the face is one of the most awesome things to have ever awesomed. Him teaming up with Kali, Sekmet, Mithra, Ogun, the Monster Slayer Twins, and Sun Wukong to fight the entire Mythos would be even more so. (There's probably some obscure manga out there where this happens.)<br /> <br /> Regarding the neurotic racism of a lot of Lovecraft's work, I highly recommend Victor LaValle's The Ballad of Black Tom, which is set around the events of &quot;The Horror at Red Hook&quot; and puts them into an entirely different perspective. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T15:02:39-08:00","id":1282522,"title":"","content":"Call me crazy, but I'm actually optimistic about this product. Granted, I've been vocal about the fact that I'm not particularly invested in even using, much less maintaining the fidelity of, the new setting, but I can understand if not truly relate to concerns from the perspective of the HPL Mythos not meshing with the new setting... however, at-least for the Origins portion of the game, the way that that new tier actually PLAYS (rather than reads) is very much in line with &quot;The Mythos.&quot; I've often described Origins tier as ideal for running games of &quot;Call of Cthulhu meets Scoobie Doo, but with Gods.&quot; An alternate setting that's intentionally centered around that particular play-style actually sounds aces. Personally, if I were running a HPL Mythos game using Origin, I probably wouldn't have the &quot;scions&quot; so much be children of The Mythos as mortals who were touched by the greater cosmos and left with a small spark of power (and probably madness.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","user":"mjorkk","date":". 01-24-2019, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1576-mjorkk","name":"mjorkk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T01:52:54-08:00","id":1283872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1280725#post1280725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> India: This being is incomprhensible because it is a thousand thousand things at once, it's body being made of all the other gods, thus containing the whole universe.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft: This being is incomprehensible because it's head is a squid. I am afraid of sea food.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No, it's incomprehensible because it represents the concept of <b>infinity</b>, something which the human brain is not properly equipped to deal with. You might, if you try hard enough, envision a being who embodies a thousand different things at once. You will never be able to imagine something that had no beginning and has no end. No matter how large you imagine the universe (or deity, or whatever) to be in scale to our world, your brain will always place subconscious boundaries and limitations on its scale and power.<br /> <br /> No matter how hard you concentrate on a singular thought, your brain will eventually become distracted by something else. Usually something more important, but perhaps not necessarily. The point is, perceiving the true scope of infinity and what that means is something we are psychologically (as well as biologically) incapable of doing.<br /> <br /> That's why people are often depicted as collapsing into a catatonic state when their mind is blasted with the concept of infinity. Its because their brain is locked onto the same thought process that goes on and on and on until they finally die and the brain starts decaying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T04:25:16-08:00","id":1283887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1283872#post1283872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's incomprehensible because it represents the concept of <b>infinity</b>, something which the human brain is not properly equipped to deal with. You might, if you try hard enough, envision a being who embodies a thousand different things at once. You will never be able to imagine something that had no beginning and has no end. No matter how large you imagine the universe (or deity, or whatever) to be in scale to our world, your brain will always place subconscious boundaries and limitations on its scale and power.<br /> <br /> No matter how hard you concentrate on a singular thought, your brain will eventually become distracted by something else. Usually something more important, but perhaps not necessarily. The point is, perceiving the true scope of infinity and what that means is something we are psychologically (as well as biologically) incapable of doing.<br /> <br /> That's why people are often depicted as collapsing into a catatonic state when their mind is blasted with the concept of infinity. Its because their brain is locked onto the same thought process that goes on and on and on until they finally die and the brain starts decaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt that anyone can imagine anything that is more than one thing at the same time in the same way. We can conceptualize a something being two things at once, but not imagine. For example, can you imagine a man that is, at the same time and in the same way, a dog? Not spiritually a dog, not mentally a dog, but full on physically man and dog. Our mind is as much as locked to imagine infinity as the idea that one thing is more than one. It is a hardware limitation, which is there for the absolute natural reason that is pointless that we are able to, and we all have to deal with it. Is not about how long you try, you simply cant.<br /> <br /> Actually, might not even be. People, as time passes, has been able to think in more different and abstract ways just by being exposed to different and abstract ideas since their minds formation. I am not even sure it is a hardware limitation, maybe it is just a natural limitation by being raised in a less abstract form of thinking, and future generations will easily imagine it in ways that I, literally, cant imagine. Who knows?<br /> <br /> But neither concept is scary. Lovecraftians beings are not scary because they are represent the concept of infinity, they are scary because they represent an unfeeling cosmos and beings so utterly more powerful that we are mere specs of nothing, which in itself has nothing to do with infinity. They might have existed since the beggining and keep being until the end, and the Blind Stupid God might exist outside our universe, but nothing of that is not the scary part. The Lovecraftian horror is mostly based on the horror of the unknown, of the existencial unimportance and the classic amorphously grotesque.<br /> <br /> And, honestly, in my opnion, the Lovecraftian mythos have lost their prime. They are not as scary, nor as interesting as they once where, specially for 21th century viewers. With a thousand media pieces creating different versions and spawning long family trees and complicated stories about those mythos, they are not and unknown as they once are. Just like the Xenomorph from Alien, as people started explaining more and more of where it came and what it does, the more it lost their scary factor. And, again, as the Xenomorph from Alien, the best way to experience it is from the original, straight from the source, trying to ignore and forget everything you know about it. It is now a piece of pop media, and nothing turns the unknown incomprehensible becoming a Meme.<br /> <br /> Funny enough, I think the mythos are more interesting without the mythos, just as general separated entities that might, or might not, have relations. Separated stories that, just because the same guy wrote (which in many cases isnt even true, as the Mythos were vastly expanded by other people than Lovecraft) doesnt mean they inhabit the same universe.<br /> <br /> Also media depicts people becoming catatonic due to infinity because it is fiction, it can do whatever it wants. Each fictional story in which it happens can have its own explanation, and in some cases people became Gods, other people became catatonic, other gains superpowers, other block part of the information. If you are arguing that it is what would happen if someone were exposed to infinity, than I dont know what to say to you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T05:47:55-08:00","id":1283896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1283872#post1283872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> No, it's incomprehensible because it represents the concept of <b>infinity</b>, something which the human brain is not properly equipped to deal with. You might, if you try hard enough, envision a being who embodies a thousand different things at once. You will never be able to imagine something that had no beginning and has no end. No matter how large you imagine the universe (or deity, or whatever) to be in scale to our world, your brain will always place subconscious boundaries and limitations on its scale and power.<br /> <br /> No matter how hard you concentrate on a singular thought, your brain will eventually become distracted by something else. Usually something more important, but perhaps not necessarily. The point is, perceiving the true scope of infinity and what that means is something we are psychologically (as well as biologically) incapable of doing.<br /> <br /> That's why people are often depicted as collapsing into a catatonic state when their mind is blasted with the concept of infinity. Its because their brain is locked onto the same thought process that goes on and on and on until they finally die and the brain starts decaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nyrufa, I'm pretty sure <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> banned you from posting on this threat, so maybe retreat instead of threatening me with the Infinite Perspective Vortex over making a joke about media I actually love. And in any case, I am also pretty sure that squid don't represent infinity to most people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T06:18:06-08:00","id":1283903,"title":"","content":"As I see... the point is not the squid head nor infinity, but the way it interact with the flow of the universe. The universe around us work on a certain way, the presence of this beings cause a \u201creality turbulence\u201d, the same way that happens to seeing a Greek god in real form, it\u2019s not the vision of the real form, but the impact it have on our concient mind.<br /> <br /> Imagine a radiation that instead of causing cancer on your body, cause \u201ccancer\u201d on your conscience (not the Brain). There is no reason to think that there is no quantifiable conscience, otherwise how does the big squid head can affect our dreams? It\u2019s not pheromones or anything like. You can go for psychic, mystic or any supernatural explanation for the conscience damage, but it\u2019s not about symbols or images.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T06:26:01-08:00","id":1283905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1283903#post1283903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I see... the point is not the squid head nor infinity, but the way it interact with the flow of the universe. The universe around us work on a certain way, the presence of this beings cause a \u201creality turbulence\u201d, the same way that happens to seeing a Greek god in real form, it\u2019s not the vision of the real form, but the impact it have on our concient mind.<br /> <br /> Imagine a radiation that instead of causing cancer on your body, cause \u201ccancer\u201d on your conscience (not the Brain). There is no reason to think that there is no quantifiable conscience, otherwise how does the big squid head can affect our dreams? It\u2019s not pheromones or anything like. You can go for psychic, mystic or any supernatural explanation for the conscience damage, but it\u2019s not about symbols or images.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, that's my point. Real world deities can mess with your mind just as much as the Old Ones, if not better. And reducing them all to &quot;afraid of seafood&quot;, was, as mentioned, a joke. ^^'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T06:57:57-08:00","id":1283914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1283896#post1283896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nyrufa, I'm pretty sure <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> banned you from posting on this threat, so maybe retreat instead of threatening me with the Infinite Perspective Vortex over making a joke about media I actually love. And in any case, I am also pretty sure that squid don't represent infinity to most people.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was neither trying to threaten you, nor make jokes. But I saw the previous quote and just felt compelled to reply with my own thought on the subject.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I'll go back to lurking in this thread's background, while we wait to hear more information about this project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T09:26:35-08:00","id":1283947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1280166-scion-mythos-officially?p=1283896#post1283896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nyrufa, I'm pretty sure <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> banned you from posting on this thread</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">I did, but next time please just report the post instead of engaging with the thread-banned user.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T19:57:09-08:00","id":1290975,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m very surprised that the Old Ones will be gods, rather than some other outside context problem. Isn\u2019t that what defines them?<br /> <br /> I guess Dragons are the \u201cthird force\u201d though. Honestly it just sound like a gimmicky ploy that Onyx Path knows will attract paying customers - which is fine because they\u2019re a business, but Lovecraft\u2019s themes of cosmic insignificance in a game of divine superstars makes it feel like they\u2019re selling out.<br /> <br /> Had it been a chapter in a Shards book? Sure, but it still seems like material better covered in a community content Vault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T22:01:01-08:00","id":1291004,"title":"","content":"Dragons are in OFFICIAL line supplement called 'Scion Dragons'. This topic is dedicated to book 'Scion - Masks of Mythos' - which will be Scion Shard. Dragons are part of official line, ( And they are from 1E, I may add.) Old Ones will be in one time Shard book. HUGE differance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T11:41:44-08:00","id":1291204,"title":"","content":"Actually I wasn\u2019t criticizing the Dragons supplement at all. I was saying how they fill a \u201cthird force\u201d already so Lovecraftian Old Ones would be redundant in that situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T04:52:28-07:00","id":1316963,"title":"","content":"I think mixing Scion and the Cthulhu Mythos could work with just a few tweaks, even without making Scions the spawn of the Great Old Ones. Here is the approach I'd take:<br /> <br /> The &quot;Outer Gods&quot; of the Mythos such as Azatoth, Shub-Niggurath, Nyarlathotep, and so forth are cosmic-scale entities similar to the Primordials. They can be warded against for a time, but never truly defeated. But the Great Old Ones such as Cthulhu, Dagon, Ghatanotoa and so forth are ultimately finite beings not on the same scale as the Outer Gods - so they can be on a similar scale as the anthromorphic Gods of Scion.<br /> <br /> But how can we reconcile the potency of the gods of human beliefs with the notions that, in the cosmology of the Cthulhu Mythos, humans are an insiginificant and ultimately doomed species? The key, I think, lies in these lines from &quot;The Call of Cthulhu&quot;:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The time would be easy to know, for then mankind would have become as the Great Old Ones; free and wild and beyond good and evil, with laws and morals thrown aside and all men shouting and killing and revelling in joy. Then the liberated Old Ones would teach them new ways to shout and kill and revel and enjoy themselves, and all the earth would flame with a holocaust of ecstasy and freedom.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> These lines can be interpreted in different ways, but to my mind this sounds like a form of Transhumanism - humans <i>can</i> become as powerful as the Great Old Ones, as long as they are willing to abandon what made them human in the first place.<br /> <br /> And ultimately, isn't this part of the very process of becoming a God in Scion? The Scions start out as mere mortals with a special spark, but the more they grow in power and the more their Legend grows, the more they have to abandon their humanity and become altogether alien entities that are connected to humans by a mere thread.<br /> <br /> And while some Gods fight to retain their connections to humanity, this is ultimately as doomed as humanity itself - once humanity has passed on, the Great Old Ones of Earth will scatter across the universe and gibbering things under alien stars too will worship entities with unspeakable names such as &quot;Tezcatlipoca&quot;, &quot;Thor&quot;, or &quot;Donnie Rhodes&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}